; A rule-level fixed/null choice owns its fixed arm through a deterministic nominal singleton, then
; uses the existing presence API: `t = true / null` becomes `Option<FixedBoolTrue>`. `Some` writes
; only `true`; `None` writes null. This preserves a fixed constraint without pretending the value is
; an unstored field-only sentinel. `null / null` is one singleton null type, not `Option<...>`, so it
; has exactly one semantic state.
;
; The member-position sibling is covered by choice_fixed_null_collapse_member.cddl. Three-or-more
; arm choices remain ordinary enums and are outside this two-arm collapse.
a = [x: uint]
t = true / null
